1
00:00:00,143 --> 00:00:02,143
(Sheldon:)And how difficult it is to do

2
00:00:02,145 --> 00:00:04,145
(Sheldon:)when she's bloated,
cranky and crampy?

3
00:00:04,147 --> 00:00:06,217
(Sheldon:)Continue.

4
00:00:08,151 --> 00:00:10,151
(Penny:)Sheldon, we are just people.

5
00:00:10,153 --> 00:00:12,353
(Penny:)We talk about the same things
you guys talk about.

6
00:00:12,355 --> 00:00:15,025
(Sheldon:)You talk about
if werewolves can swim?

7
00:00:15,025 --> 00:00:16,655
(Sheldon:)See, Leonard says yes,

8
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,490
(Sheldon:)but I say it depends on
if the human could swim

9
00:00:19,496 --> 00:00:20,496
(Sheldon:)before he was bitten.

10
00:00:20,497 --> 00:00:21,897
(Sheldon:)What do you think?

11
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:25,833
(Penny:)Let's just talk
about our periods.

12
00:00:25,836 --> 00:00:27,706
(Amy:)No, hold on.

13
00:00:27,704 --> 00:00:30,704
(Amy:)All canines instinctively know
how to swim.

14
00:00:30,707 --> 00:00:33,337
(Amy:)Why wouldn't a werewolf have
the same abilities?

15
00:00:33,343 --> 00:00:35,913
(Bernadette:)Well, they're not
a hundred percent wolf.

16
00:00:35,912 --> 00:00:38,682
(Bernadette:)They're a werewolf--
that's only part wolf.

17
00:00:38,682 --> 00:00:40,682
(Bernadette:)It's like comparing
apples to oranges.

18
00:00:40,684 --> 00:00:42,714
(Sheldon:)Thank you.

19
00:00:42,719 --> 00:00:45,349
(Sheldon:)Oh, and technically, it's apples
that turn into were-oranges

20
00:00:45,355 --> 00:00:46,755
(Sheldon:)when the moon is full.

21
00:00:48,058 --> 00:00:50,388
(Sheldon:)Hey, this is fun.

22
00:00:50,393 --> 00:00:52,523
(Sheldon:)We should do it sometime
when you aren't all PMS'ing.

23
00:00:52,529 --> 00:00:53,759
(Leonard:)Bye.

24
00:00:57,033 --> 00:01:02,023
(Darth Vader breathes, the Joker
laughs, Godzilla roars)

